{"cti_reasoning":"With pend=win=1, stg=0 and cnt=1, P holds because the sampled cnt is nonzero. R is violated because cnt+stg=1, not 4. With en=0 the design holds this state indefinitely. One enabled step (stg!=3) moves to stg=1, cnt=0 with pend and win still set. On the following cycle $past(en), $past(win) and $past(pend) are all true but $past(cnt)==0, so P fails.","cti_state":[{"signal":"win","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"pend","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"stg","value":"64'd0"},{"signal":"cnt","value":"64'd1"},{"signal":"tos","value":"2'd1"},{"signal":"pv","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"ras0","value":"64'd0"},{"signal":"ras1","value":"64'd0"},{"signal":"ret_addr","value":"64'd0"},{"signal":"ret_valid","value":"1'b0"}],"invariants":["win == pend","!pend || (stg <= 64'd3 && cnt + stg == 64'd4)","tos <= 2'd2"],"verilog":"module ras_walker (
