{"cti_reasoning":"With armed=1, idx=255 and wreg=0, P holds vacuously because idx is not 256. R requires wreg == wexp == K^255 mod M, which is nonzero because M is prime and K is a unit, so R is false. With en=0 the state holds for any number of cycles; one accepted chunk then sets idx=256 and wreg=(0*K)%M=0, which differs from C and breaks P.","cti_state":[{"signal":"armed","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"idx","value":"9'd255"},{"signal":"wreg","value":"64'd0"},{"signal":"acc","value":"64'd0"},{"signal":"en","value":"1'b0"},{"signal":"rst","value":"1'b0"}],"invariants":["idx <= 9'd256","wreg == wexp"],"verilog":"module lim_mod_fold (
