{"cti_reasoning":"The state has phase=DECODE with leaf_idx=7, started_seen=0, armed_seen=0 and pre_abort=1. It satisfies P because phase is not DONE, so the guard is false. It violates R because DECODE requires started_seen && armed_seen. With en low the design holds this state indefinitely. One cycle with en=1, abort=0 and rst=0 finishes the last leaf, so phase becomes DONE while pre_abort=1 and started_seen=0, which breaks P.","cti_state":[{"signal":"phase","value":"2'd2"},{"signal":"leaf_idx","value":"3'd7"},{"signal":"started_seen","value":"1'b0"},{"signal":"armed_seen","value":"1'b0"},{"signal":"pre_abort","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"ps","value":"8'd0"},{"signal":"dec","value":"8'd0"}],"invariants":["!started_seen || armed_seen","!(phase == 2'd2 || phase == 2'd3) || (started_seen && armed_seen)","!(phase == 2'd1) || armed_seen"],"verilog":"module polar_sc_result_dec (
