{"cti_reasoning":"With occ=8 and wptr=rptr=0, P (occ<=8) holds, but R fails because occ is 8 while the pointer fill is 0. The design idles here as long as i_ce and i_pop are low. Because full is computed from the pointers, the log looks empty, so one enabled NaN operation is accepted as a push and occ becomes 9, violating P.","cti_state":[{"signal":"occ","value":"16'd8"},{"signal":"wptr","value":"4'd0"},{"signal":"rptr","value":"4'd0"},{"signal":"fill","value":"4'd0"}],"invariants":["occ == {12'd0, fill}","fill <= 4'd8"],"verilog":"module nan_canon_log (
