{"cti_reasoning":"The CTI has both blocks dirty, a dirty count of 1 and the summary flag set. P holds because any_dirty is 1 and the count is nonzero. R is violated because the count should equal the popcount of the dirty bits, which is 2. With i_ce low the RAM idles there indefinitely. One clear of block 0 then decrements the count to 0 while block 1 stays dirty, so any_dirty is recomputed as 1 against a zero count and P fails.","cti_state":[{"signal":"dirty","value":"2'b11"},{"signal":"dirty_cnt","value":"2'd1"},{"signal":"any_dirty","value":"1'b1"}],"invariants":["dirty_cnt == {1'b0, dirty[0]} + {1'b0, dirty[1]}","any_dirty == (dirty[0] | dirty[1])"],"verilog":"module dirty_track_ram (
