{"cti_reasoning":"S has oe=1 and we=0 while the phase is SETUP (2'd1) with a write latched (wr_lat=1). It satisfies P because oe and we are not both high, and with i_ce low it holds S indefinitely. It violates R because oe is high outside ACCESS and oe is high while wr_lat=1. With cnt at its maximum the setup compare passes on the next enabled cycle, so the controller enters ACCESS and sets we without clearing oe. The cycle after that, the $past check sees oe and we both high.","cti_state":[{"signal":"phase","value":"2'd1"},{"signal":"oe","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"we","value":"1'b0"},{"signal":"wr_lat","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"cnt","value":"64'hFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF"},{"signal":"cs_lat","value":"5'd0"},{"signal":"armed","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"pv","value":"1'b1"}],"invariants":["!(oe || we) || phase == 2'd2","!oe || !wr_lat","!we || wr_lat"],"verilog":"module async_mem_bus_ctrl (
