{"cti_reasoning":"With armed=1, frame_cnt=8, bin_idx=127 and samples_left=5, the last sampled frame count (8) is within the bound, so P holds. The relation fails because 8*128+127+5=1156, not 1024. With in_valid and dump low the design idles there forever. One accepted sample then wraps bin_idx and raises frame_cnt to 9, so on the next cycle $past(frame_cnt)=9 exceeds 8 while armed is still high.","cti_state":[{"signal":"armed","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"pv","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"frame_cnt","value":"8'd8"},{"signal":"bin_idx","value":"8'd127"},{"signal":"samples_left","value":"11'd5"},{"signal":"$past(frame_cnt)","value":"8'd8"}],"invariants":["bin_idx <= 8'd127","!armed || (({3'b000, frame_cnt, 7'b0000000}) + {10'd0, bin_idx} + {7'd0, samples_left}) == 18'd1024"],"verilog":"module welch_spectral_avg (
