{"cti_reasoning":"With armed=1, sig_a=64'h8000000000000000 and sig_b=64'hFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF, the low bytes agree (sig_a[7:0]=8'h00 and ~sig_b[7:0]=8'h00), so P holds. R is violated because ~sig_b is 0, which differs from sig_a in bit 63. With ce, start and stop all low the design idles in this state indefinitely. One ce step with din=0 shifts out bit 63 of lane A only, so lane A picks up the feedback polynomial and becomes 64'h1B while lane B's true value stays 0. The low bytes then differ (8'h1B vs 8'h00) and P fails.","cti_state":[{"signal":"armed","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"sig_a","value":"64'h8000000000000000"},{"signal":"sig_b","value":"64'hFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF"}],"invariants":["sig_b == ~sig_a"],"verilog":"module misr_lockstep (
    input  wire        clk,
    input  wire        rst,
    input  wire        ce,
    input  wire        start,
    input  wire        stop,
