{"cti_reasoning":"S holds carry_q=1 while the low half of cnt is zero, so the registered carry disagrees with cnt[31:0], violating R. Holding i_ce low keeps every register (and therefore every $stable/$past sample) unchanged, so P holds trivially across any stall window. One enabled step then increments epoch because carry_q is 1, while cnt[63:32] stays put because the low half is not all-ones. The high half is stable but epoch changed, so P fails.","cti_state":[{"signal":"cnt","value":"64'h0000000000000000"},{"signal":"carry_q","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"epoch","value":"64'h0000000000000000"},{"signal":"armed","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"pv","value":"1'b1"}],"invariants":["carry_q == (cnt[31:0] == 32'hFFFFFFFF)"],"verilog":"module mcycle_epoch (
