{"cti_reasoning":"S satisfies P because finish_seen is 0, so the guard q_seen && finish_seen is false. S violates R because the FSM is in RUN (st=2) while start_seen and armed_seen are both 0. With ce low the design holds S indefinitely; one ce step with out_cnt=11 moves st to DONE and sets finish_seen, while start_seen stays 0, so P fails.","cti_state":[{"signal":"q_seen","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"st","value":"2'd2"},{"signal":"out_cnt","value":"4'd11"},{"signal":"armed_seen","value":"1'b0"},{"signal":"start_seen","value":"1'b0"},{"signal":"finish_seen","value":"1'b0"},{"signal":"fill","value":"5'd24"},{"signal":"phase","value":"5'd0"}],"invariants":["st == 2'd0 || armed_seen","st < 2'd2 || start_seen","!start_seen || armed_seen","!finish_seen || start_seen","fill <= 5'd24","phase < 5'd24","out_cnt <= 4'd11"],"verilog":"module polyphase_resampler (
