{"cti_reasoning":"With phase=IDLE, step_cnt=2 and fin_q=0, P holds vacuously because fin_q is low. R is violated because step_cnt should equal phase (2 != 0). Holding i_ce low leaves this state unchanged indefinitely. One i_ce-high step then sets fin_q from step_cnt==2 while the previous phase was IDLE, so a finish appears without a preceding start and P fails.","cti_state":[{"signal":"phase","value":"2'd0"},{"signal":"step_cnt","value":"32'd2"},{"signal":"fin_q","value":"1'b0"},{"signal":"pv","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"$past(phase)","value":"2'd0"}],"invariants":["step_cnt == {30'd0, phase}","fin_q == (phase == 2'd3)"],"verilog":"module usb_route_lookup (
