{"cti_reasoning":"S satisfies P because fault is low and was low last cycle, so it has not risen. S violates R because both pipeline flags hit_q and miss_q are set. With i_ce low the design holds S indefinitely; one enabled step copies both flags into grant and fault, so fault rises while grant is high and P fails.","cti_state":[{"signal":"pv","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"pre_lock","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"hit_q","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"miss_q","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"grant","value":"1'b0"},{"signal":"fault","value":"1'b0"},{"signal":"$past(fault)","value":"1'b0"}],"invariants":["!(hit_q && miss_q)","!(grant && fault)"],"verilog":"module mpu_region_checker (
