{"cti_reasoning":"With armed=1, base=0, cur_addr=1023, line=0 and px=0, the offset cur_addr-base is 1023, so P holds. R is violated because base+(line<<5)+px is 0, not 1023. Holding ce low keeps every register unchanged, so the design can idle here. One ce step then takes px to 1 (no end-of-line) and cur_addr to 1024, so the offset becomes 1024 and P fails.","cti_state":[{"signal":"armed","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"base","value":"32'd0"},{"signal":"cur_addr","value":"32'd1023"},{"signal":"line","value":"32'd0"},{"signal":"px","value":"32'd0"}],"invariants":["px < 32'd32","line < 32'd32","cur_addr == base + (line << 5) + px"],"verilog":"module fb_scanout (
