{"cti_reasoning":"The window is open (armed=1) and occ is 9, so P (occ <= 9) holds, but every valid bit in the chain is zero, so occ does not equal the popcount of the chain and R is violated. With i_ce low every register holds, so the design can sit in this state for any number of cycles. One shift with i_ce=1, i_vld=1 and i_sof=i_eof=0 raises occ to 10 while armed stays 1, which violates P.","cti_state":[{"signal":"armed","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"occ","value":"64'd9"},{"signal":"a_v","value":"4'b0000"},{"signal":"lk_v","value":"1'b0"},{"signal":"b_v","value":"4'b0000"}],"invariants":["occ == a_v[0] + a_v[1] + a_v[2] + a_v[3] + lk_v + b_v[0] + b_v[1] + b_v[2] + b_v[3]"],"verilog":"module axis_scan_lockup (
