{"cti_reasoning":"S has armed=1 and the carry-save pair (sum_r=1, carry_r=0) resolving to 1, so the CSA-zero flag is low and P holds. The binary shadow acc=2 disagrees with the resolved value 1, so R (acc == sum_r + carry_r<<1) is false. With i_ce low every register holds, so the design idles in S. One enabled step with i_byte=8'hFF and i_close=0 gives sum_r=8'hFE and carry_r=8'h01, which resolve to 0, while acc becomes 8'h01. The zero flag and the busy flag are then both set while armed is still 1, so P fails.","cti_state":[{"signal":"armed","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"sum_r","value":"8'd1"},{"signal":"carry_r","value":"8'd0"},{"signal":"acc","value":"8'd2"}],"invariants":["acc == sum_r + {carry_r[6:0], 1'b0}"],"verilog":"module csa_token_checksum (
