{"cti_reasoning":"With win=1, pend=1, cd=1, step=3 the property holds because cd is nonzero, but R fails because cd+step is 4 rather than 8. Holding en low keeps this state indefinitely. One en cycle then sets cd to 0 and step to 4; pend stays 1 because step was not 7, and win stays 1, so P fails in the successor.","cti_state":[{"signal":"win","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"pend","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"cd","value":"64'd1"},{"signal":"step","value":"64'd3"}],"invariants":["!pend || (cd + step == 64'd8)","!pend || (step <= 64'd7)"],"verilog":"module axis_luma_compressor (
