{"cti_reasoning":"State pre_ev=1, busy=1, idx=4, cnt=1 satisfies P because cnt is nonzero and idx is below 16. It violates R, which requires cnt == 3 when idx == 4. With en low the design holds this state for as long as the induction window needs. One enabled step without fuse_reload takes the non-completing branch (idx != 12), giving idx=8 and cnt=0 while still busy, so P fails.","cti_state":[{"signal":"pre_ev","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"busy","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"idx","value":"5'd4"},{"signal":"cnt","value":"64'd1"},{"signal":"hit","value":"1'b0"},{"signal":"en","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"rst","value":"1'b0"},{"signal":"fuse_reload","value":"1'b0"}],"invariants":["!(pre_ev && busy) || (idx[1:0] == 2'b00)","!(pre_ev && busy) || (idx <= 5'd12)","!(pre_ev && busy) || (cnt == 64'd4 - {61'd0, idx[4:2]})"],"verilog":"module hack_rowfix (
