{"cti_reasoning":"With win=0 the antecedent of P is false, so P holds even though corr_cnt=5 while inj_seen=0. That pairing, along with err_flag=1, violates R. Holding en=0 freezes every register, so the design can idle in this state for any depth. One step with en=1 and scrub_start=1 then sets win=1 while corr_cnt stays 5 (the engine was idle in that cycle) and inj_seen stays 0, so P fails.","cti_state":[{"signal":"win","value":"1'b0"},{"signal":"inj_seen","value":"1'b0"},{"signal":"inj_cnt","value":"32'd0"},{"signal":"corr_cnt","value":"32'd5"},{"signal":"err_flag","value":"16'h0001"},{"signal":"scan_ptr","value":"4'd0"},{"signal":"syn_reg","value":"12'h000"}],"invariants":["inj_seen || (corr_cnt == 32'd0)","inj_seen || (err_flag == 16'h0000)"],"verilog":"module golay_scrub (
    input  wire        clk,
    input  wire        rst,
