{"cti_reasoning":"The state idx=255, dn=5, win=1 satisfies P because idx<=255. It violates R because idx+dn = 260, not 255. With en=0 (and rst=0) it holds indefinitely. One step with en=1 and line_start=1 keeps win=1 and moves idx to 256, because the wrap tests only dn and dn!=0. That successor violates P.","cti_state":[{"signal":"idx","value":"32'd255"},{"signal":"dn","value":"32'd5"},{"signal":"win","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"y","value":"32'd0"}],"invariants":["idx + dn == 32'd255","dn <= 32'd255"],"verilog":"module hdmi_line_window (
    input  wire        clk,
