{"cti_reasoning":"With win=1, phase=ARMED and arm_cnt=start_cnt=fin_cnt=5, P holds vacuously because phase is not STARTED. R is violated because the ARMED clause requires arm_cnt==start_cnt+1. Holding en=0 keeps this state for any number of cycles. Then en=1 with mutex_gnt=1 and eof=0 moves to phase=STARTED with start_cnt=6 and arm_cnt=5 while win stays 1, which breaks P's arm_cnt==start_cnt.","cti_state":[{"signal":"win","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"phase","value":"2'd1"},{"signal":"hs_latch","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"clk_en","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"arm_cnt","value":"32'd5"},{"signal":"start_cnt","value":"32'd5"},{"signal":"fin_cnt","value":"32'd5"},{"signal":"wptr","value":"8'd0"}],"invariants":["phase != 2'd0 || (arm_cnt == start_cnt && start_cnt == fin_cnt && clk_en && !hs_latch)","phase != 2'd1 || (arm_cnt == start_cnt + 32'd1 && start_cnt == fin_cnt && clk_en && hs_latch)","phase != 2'd2 || (arm_cnt == start_cnt && start_cnt == fin_cnt + 32'd1 && !clk_en && hs_latch)","phase != 2'd3"],"verilog":"module jls_pausible_clkctl (
