{"cti_reasoning":"S satisfies P because finished=0. It violates R because started=1 while armed=0. With en=0 every register holds, so the design can idle in S indefinitely. Then one enabled cycle with rx equal to samp[0] (no edge, so no slip) sets finished, since started=1 and bit_cnt==383. In the successor no_slip=1, finished=1 and $past(armed)=0, so P fails.","cti_state":[{"signal":"armed","value":"1'b0"},{"signal":"started","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"finished","value":"1'b0"},{"signal":"bit_cnt","value":"16'd383"},{"signal":"no_slip","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"pv","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"$past(armed)","value":"1'b0"},{"signal":"samp","value":"4'b0000"},{"signal":"phase_sel","value":"2'd0"},{"signal":"os_cnt","value":"2'd0"},{"signal":"vote","value":"3'b000"},{"signal":"prev_bit","value":"1'b0"},{"signal":"en","value":"1'b0"}],"invariants":["!started || armed","!finished || started","(bit_cnt == 16'd0) || started","bit_cnt <= 16'd383"],"verilog":"module doomsday_cdr (
    input wire clk,
    input wire rst,
    input wire en,
    input wire rx,
