{"cti_reasoning":"S has win=1, acc_seen=1, ph=0 and occ=254. It satisfies P: A1 is vacuous because acc_seen=1, and A2 is vacuous because ph=0. It violates R because {ph,1'b0}=0, not 254. With en=0 the design holds S indefinitely. One step with en=1 and in_v=1 (no sof, not a stall) gives occ=254+2, which wraps to 0, and ph=1, so A2 (win && acc_seen && ph!=0 => occ!=0) fails.","cti_state":[{"signal":"win","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"acc_seen","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"ph","value":"7'd0"},{"signal":"occ","value":"8'd254"},{"signal":"gbuf","value":"256'd0"},{"signal":"out_v","value":"1'b0"},{"signal":"out_word","value":"128'd0"}],"invariants":["occ == {ph, 1'b0}","ph <= 7'd64"],"verilog":"module vid_gearbox_128b130b (
