{"cti_reasoning":"With armed=1, busy=1, iter=0 and remaining=1, P holds because remaining is not zero. R is violated because iter + remaining = 1, not 32. Holding ce low freezes every register, so the design can idle here indefinitely. One ce cycle (start=0, ack=0) then performs a micro-rotation: iter becomes 1 and remaining becomes 0. Busy stays high because iter was not 31, and armed stays high, so busy && remaining==0 holds in the armed window and P fails.","cti_state":[{"signal":"armed","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"busy","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"done","value":"1'b0"},{"signal":"iter","value":"64'd0"},{"signal":"remaining","value":"64'd1"},{"signal":"x","value":"64'd0"},{"signal":"y","value":"64'd0"},{"signal":"z","value":"64'd0"}],"invariants":["iter + remaining == 64'd32","!busy || iter < 64'd32"],"verilog":"module cordic_rot64 (
