{"cti_reasoning":"With armed=1, tx_cnt=11 and rx_cnt=10, neither absence assertion fires: tx_sof and rx_eof are both 0, and rx_sof is 0. The state breaks R because tx_cnt != rx_cnt. With i_ce low it idles there forever. One i_ce step then wraps tx_cnt to 0 and moves rx_cnt to 11, so tx_sof and rx_eof are both high and the first assertion fails.","cti_state":[{"signal":"armed","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"tx_cnt","value":"32'd11"},{"signal":"rx_cnt","value":"32'd10"},{"signal":"lfsr_tx","value":"32'h1D2C3B4A"},{"signal":"lfsr_rx","value":"32'h1D2C3B4A"}],"invariants":["tx_cnt == rx_cnt","tx_cnt <= 32'd11","lfsr_tx == lfsr_rx"],"verilog":"module frame_scrambler32 (
