{"cti_reasoning":"In S the scan is armed and still before its first frame wrap. Bit 30 of the anode is lit and visited_hi is 0, so anode[31] is low and P holds. S violates R because the one-hot anode (bit 30) does not match dig_idx=5, which demands bit 5. With i_ce low the scanner idles in S indefinitely. One scan tick then rotates the anode to bit 31 while visited_hi stays 0, since anode[16] was never lit, and armed stays 1, since dig_idx is not 31. The last digit is now driven without digit 16 ever having been driven, so P fails.","cti_state":[{"signal":"dig_idx","value":"32'd5"},{"signal":"anode","value":"32'h40000000"},{"signal":"visited_hi","value":"1'b0"},{"signal":"armed","value":"1'b1"}],"invariants":["dig_idx <= 32'd31","anode == (32'd1 << dig_idx)","!armed || (visited_hi == (dig_idx > 32'd16))"],"verilog":"module sevenseg_scan_mux (
