{"cti_reasoning":"With phase=2 (bypass/started) P holds trivially because the guard needs phase==3. R is violated because phase==2 requires start_seen=1 but start_seen is 0. With ce low the design idles here forever. One cycle with ce and finish high moves phase to 3 while $past(start_seen) is 0, so P fails.","cti_state":[{"signal":"pv","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"win","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"phase","value":"2'd2"},{"signal":"arm_seen","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"start_seen","value":"1'b0"},{"signal":"stored","value":"32'd0"},{"signal":"xact_cnt","value":"32'd0"}],"invariants":["(phase != 2'd0) || (!arm_seen && !start_seen)","(phase != 2'd1) || (arm_seen && !start_seen)","(phase != 2'd2) || (arm_seen && start_seen)","(phase != 2'd3) || (arm_seen && start_seen)"],"verilog":"module bypass_xact_reg (
