{"cti_reasoning":"With before_mute=1, acc=16'h8000, acc_chk=16'h0000 and dout=dchk=0, P holds because both outputs are stable while ce and mute are low, so the design can idle here forever. The state violates R because acc != acc_chk while still before the first mute. One ce step with din=16'h8000 carries out of the main accumulator, so dout rises to 1. The check accumulator does not carry, so dchk stays 0. dchk is therefore stable while dout changed, which breaks P.","cti_state":[{"signal":"before_mute","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"pv","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"acc","value":"16'h8000"},{"signal":"acc_chk","value":"16'h0000"},{"signal":"dout","value":"1'b0"},{"signal":"dchk","value":"1'b0"},{"signal":"din","value":"16'h8000"},{"signal":"ce","value":"1'b0 while stalling, then 1'b1"},{"signal":"mute","value":"1'b0"}],"invariants":["!before_mute || (acc == acc_chk)","!before_mute || (dout == dchk)"],"verilog":"module sd_dac_lockstep (
