{"cti_reasoning": "In state S the FSM register holds the unreachable encoding 3'b101 while both status flags are clear, so P (never loading and ready together) holds; S violates R because 101 is not one of the five legal encodings. With i_ce low the design sits in S for arbitrarily many cycles, and one step with i_ce high takes the default case arm, which latches loading<=1 and ready<=1 simultaneously, breaking P.", "cti_state": [{"signal": "st", "value": "3'b101"}, {"signal": "loading", "value": "1'b0"}, {"signal": "ready", "value": "1'b0"}, {"signal": "rows", "value": "4'd0"}], "invariants": ["st == 3'b000 || st == 3'b001 || st == 3'b010 || st == 3'b011 || st == 3'b100", "loading == (st == 3'b001 || st == 3'b010 || st == 3'b011)", "ready == (st == 3'b100)"], "verilog": "module vd_sheet_loader (
