{"cti_reasoning": "The stage-1 pipeline state s1_req_lo=1 together with s1_pri_hi=1 is impossible by construction (s1_pri_hi is loaded as req_hi && !req_lo in the same cycle that s1_req_lo is loaded as req_lo), so this state violates R; it satisfies P because o_vld is 0 so the guard does not fire (and both grant flags are 0 anyway). With i_ce low the design sits in this state for arbitrarily many cycles, and one cycle of i_ce=1 latches o_vld<=s1_vld=1, o_grant_lo<=s1_vld&&s1_req_lo=1 and o_grant_hi<=s1_vld&&s1_pri_hi=1, so both grants are asserted while valid is set and P fails.", "cti_state": [{"signal": "s1_vld", "value": "1'b1"}, {"signal": "s1_req_lo", "value": "1'b1"}, {"signal": "s1_req_hi", "value": "1'b1"}, {"signal": "s1_pri_hi", "value": "1'b1"}, {"signal": "s1_idx", "value": "3'd0"}, {"signal": "o_vld", "value": "1'b0"}, {"signal": "o_idx", "value": "3'd0"}, {"signal": "o_grant_lo", "value": "1'b0"}, {"signal": "o_grant_hi", "value": "1'b0"}], "invariants": ["!(s1_pri_hi && s1_req_lo)", "!s1_pri_hi || s1_req_hi"], "verilog": "// Priority arbiter for per-subchannel energy detect flags.
