{"cti_reasoning": "State S has lfsr = 5'd0 (the LFSR lockup state that the feedback structure can never actually reach) with gnt = 2'b01, so the property holds right now (only one grant is asserted) but the relation lfsr != 0 is violated; holding i_ce low lets the design sit in S forever, and one enabled step latches sel = 2'b11 into gnt, asserting both grants and breaking the property.", "cti_state": [{"signal": "lfsr", "value": "5'd0"}, {"signal": "gnt", "value": "2'b01"}, {"signal": "i_ce", "value": "1'b0"}, {"signal": "rst", "value": "1'b0"}], "invariants": ["lfsr != 5'd0"], "verilog": "module lfsr_grant_arb (
