{"cti_reasoning": "In state S the window is open, the engine claims to be busy but the beats-remaining counter has already hit zero while the drained flag is still low, so P (never busy and drained together) holds, yet the structural relation busy == (beats_left != 0) is false. The design can sit in S indefinitely with i_ce low; one step with i_ce=1, i_ack=0 takes the busy branch, which sets drained <= (beats_left <= 1) = 1 but keeps busy <= (beats_left != 1) = 1, so the next cycle has busy && drained inside the still-open window and P fails.", "cti_state": [{"signal": "beats_left", "value": "4'd0"}, {"signal": "busy", "value": "1'b1"}, {"signal": "drained", "value": "1'b0"}, {"signal": "win", "value": "1'b1"}], "invariants": ["busy == (beats_left != 4'd0)", "drained == (beats_left == 4'd0)"], "verilog": "module dma_burst_window (
