{"cti_reasoning": "State S has the skid slot occupied (stall=1) with skid=8'h01 but its shadow parity bit skid_par=0, which violates the by-construction relation skid_par == ^skid while stall is up; both asserted relations (o_par == ^o_data and acc_par == ^acc_data) currently hold because the output and accumulator registers are all zero, and with i_ce=0 the design sits in S forever. One step with i_ce=1 and i_dready=1 releases the skid word: o_data becomes 8'h01 with o_par still 0, and acc_data becomes 8'h01 with acc_par still 0, so both assertions fail in the very next state while the window register win is still 1.", "cti_state": [{"signal": "stall", "value": "1'b1"}, {"signal": "skid", "value": "8'h01"}, {"signal": "skid_par", "value": "1'b0"}, {"signal": "o_valid", "value": "1'b1"}, {"signal": "o_data", "value": "8'h00"}, {"signal": "o_par", "value": "1'b0"}, {"signal": "acc_data", "value": "8'h00"}, {"signal": "acc_par", "value": "1'b0"}, {"signal": "win", "value": "1'b1"}], "invariants": ["!stall || (skid_par == (^skid))", "!stall || o_valid"], "verilog": "module skid_parity_window (
