{"cti_reasoning": "In state S the arming register is set and the shift register holds a single in-flight token at stage 2 (pipe=4'b0100) while the occupancy counter reads 0, so the relation occ == popcount(pipe) is violated, yet the property holds because the guard needs pipe[3] (the drain stage) to be set and it is not. With i_ce low the design freezes in S for arbitrarily many cycles; one step with i_ce=1 and i_issue=0 shifts the token into the drain stage (pipe=4'b1000) while occ stays 0 and armed stays 1, and the next evaluation of the guarded check asserts occ != 0 on a retirement with zero recorded occupancy, which fails.", "cti_state": [{"signal": "pipe", "value": "4'b0100"}, {"signal": "occ", "value": "3'd0"}, {"signal": "armed", "value": "1'b1"}, {"signal": "sh_occ", "value": "3'd1"}], "invariants": ["occ == (pipe[0] + pipe[1] + pipe[2] + pipe[3])", "!armed || sh_occ != 3'd0"], "verilog": "module serv_inflight_tracker (
