{"cti_reasoning": "S has the FSM in the one-hot IDLE state but with the frame phase counter already loaded with 1 (nbits==4'd1), which satisfies P (while rx is held high nothing moves, so both nbits and st are stable and nbits<=10) yet violates the invariant clause that ties st[0] to nbits==4'd0. The design can idle in S indefinitely (rx=1, or ce=0), and one step with ce=1 and rx=0 takes the start-bit detection path: st changes from IDLE to START while the counter is *loaded* with the constant 4'd1 and therefore does not change, so $stable(nbits) holds while $stable(st) fails and P breaks.", "cti_state": [{"signal": "st", "value": "11'b000_0000_0001"}, {"signal": "nbits", "value": "4'd1"}, {"signal": "pv", "value": "1'b1"}, {"signal": "sr", "value": "8'h00"}, {"signal": "ferr", "value": "1'b0"}], "invariants": ["st != 11'd0", "(st & (st - 11'd1)) == 11'd0", "nbits <= 4'd10", "!st[0] || nbits == 4'd0", "!st[1] || nbits == 4'd1", "!st[2] || nbits == 4'd2", "!st[3] || nbits == 4'd3", "!st[4] || nbits == 4'd4", "!st[5] || nbits == 4'd5", "!st[6] || nbits == 4'd6", "!st[7] || nbits == 4'd7", "!st[8] || nbits == 4'd8", "!st[9] || nbits == 4'd9", "!st[10] || nbits == 4'd10"], "verilog": "module uart_rx_onehot (
    input  wire       clk,
    input  wire       rst,
    input  wire       ce,      // baud tick / enable: low freezes all state
    input  wire       rx,
    input  wire       take,    // consumer accepts the byte parked in STOP
