{"cti_reasoning": "In S the design is idling (issue=retire=0) with pre_deep still high, past retired_cnt equal to current retired_cnt, and issued_cnt - $past(retired_cnt) = 3, so P holds and can hold for arbitrarily many idle cycles; S violates R because outstanding is 0 while issued_cnt - retired_cnt is 3. One enabled issue step (allowed since outstanding < 4, and pre_deep stays high because outstanding was only 0) makes issued_cnt = 4 while $past(retired_cnt) is still 0, so the next state has issued_cnt - $past(retired_cnt) = 4 > 3 and P fails.", "cti_state": [{"signal": "issued_cnt", "value": "4'd3"}, {"signal": "retired_cnt", "value": "4'd0"}, {"signal": "$past(retired_cnt)", "value": "4'd0"}, {"signal": "outstanding", "value": "3'd0"}, {"signal": "pre_deep", "value": "1'b1"}, {"signal": "pv", "value": "1'b1"}], "invariants": ["outstanding <= 3'd4", "(issued_cnt - retired_cnt) == {1'b0, outstanding}", "!pre_deep || outstanding <= 3'd3"], "verilog": "module stack_scoreboard (
    input  wire       clk,
    input  wire       issue,      // a transaction is pushed onto the shadow stack
    input  wire       retire,     // a transaction is popped / completed
    output wire [2:0] outstanding_o,
    output wire       pre_deep_o
);
    // window depth of the in-flight scoreboard
    localparam [2:0] WINDOW = 3'd4;

    // free-running census of issued and retired transactions (wrap mod 16)
    reg [3:0] issued_cnt  = 4'd0;
    reg [3:0] retired_cnt = 4'd0;

    // in-flight occupancy of the window
    reg [2:0] outstanding = 3'd0;

    // "before R" arming register: starts high, cleared the first time the
    // scoreboard occupancy ever reaches 3 (the deep-stack event)
