{"cti_reasoning": "The state register is 3 bits but only encodings 0..4 are used; the CTI sits in the unreachable encoding 3'd6 with cleared_seen=0, which satisfies P vacuously (state is not PRESENT) but violates R's legal-encoding clause. With i_ce low the FSM holds 3'd6 for any number of cycles, and one step with i_ce high takes the default branch straight to PRESENT while cleared_seen stays 0, so P fails.", "cti_state": [{"signal": "state", "value": "3'd6"}, {"signal": "cleared_seen", "value": "1'b0"}, {"signal": "draw_cnt", "value": "2'd0"}], "invariants": ["state == 3'd0 || state == 3'd1 || state == 3'd2 || state == 3'd3 || state == 3'd4", "!(state == 3'd2 || state == 3'd3 || state == 3'd4) || cleared_seen"], "verilog": "module gfx_frame_fsm (
    input  wire clk,
