{"cti_reasoning":"In the state wsel=0, rsel=0, wcnt=1, rcnt=2 the two physical addresses are {0,01}=3'b001 and {0,10}=3'b010, so they differ and P holds, but the ping-pong relation wsel!=rsel is violated. With wr_en and rd_en low the design sits in this state indefinitely (swap needs wcnt==4 && rcnt==4), and one cycle with wr_en=1 advances wcnt to 2, making the write address equal the read address and breaking P.","cti_state":[{"signal":"wsel","value":"1'b0"},{"signal":"rsel","value":"1'b0"},{"signal":"wcnt","value":"3'd1"},{"signal":"rcnt","value":"3'd2"}],"invariants":["wsel != rsel","wcnt <= 3'd4","rcnt <= 3'd4"],"verilog":"module pingpong_double_buffer (
