{"cti_reasoning":"In the CTI the occupancy counter says one entry is outstanding while the pointers are equal, so the derived `empty` flag is true and the forced-service pop is suppressed; the property holds there because timer==1 is nonzero, but the relation count == (wptr-rptr) is false. With step low the design sits in this state forever, and one step with step high drives the countdown to zero while count stays at 1, so the outstanding request's deadline expires and P fails.","cti_state":[{"signal":"count","value":"3'd1"},{"signal":"wptr","value":"3'd0"},{"signal":"rptr","value":"3'd0"},{"signal":"timer","value":"3'd1"}],"invariants":["count <= 3'd4","count == ((wptr - rptr) & 3'h7)","timer <= 3'd4"],"verilog":"module fifo_deadline #(parameter DW = 8) (
