{"cti_reasoning":"The state occ=8, hiwater=8 with both pointers and both gray shadows at zero satisfies P (occ<=8 and hiwater<=8) but violates R, since R demands occ == wbin-rbin = 0; with push=pop=0 the design sits in this state forever. Because wgray==rgray the full flag is deasserted (full needs wgray=={~rgray[3:2],rgray[1:0]}=4'b1100), so one cycle with push=1 performs a real push and occ becomes 4'd9 (and hiwater 4'd9), breaking both assertions.","cti_state":[{"signal":"occ","value":"4'd8"},{"signal":"hiwater","value":"4'd8"},{"signal":"wbin","value":"4'd0"},{"signal":"rbin","value":"4'd0"},{"signal":"wgray","value":"4'b0000"},{"signal":"rgray","value":"4'b0000"}],"invariants":["wgray == (wbin ^ (wbin >> 1))","rgray == (rbin ^ (rbin >> 1))","occ == ((wbin - rbin) & 4'hF)"],"verilog":"// Instruction-fetch queue occupancy tracker with gray-coded pointers.
