{"cti_reasoning":"The state sum_h=30, car_h=0, n=0 satisfies P because the carry-save halves sum to 30, exactly the bound, but it violates R since R requires total <= 3*n = 0 when no increments have been consumed. With ce low the design sits in this state indefinitely; one enabled step with inc=3 is still inside the budget (n<10), so the CSA update produces sum_h=29, car_h=4, total=33, breaking P.","cti_state":[{"signal":"sum_h","value":"8'd30"},{"signal":"car_h","value":"8'd0"},{"signal":"n","value":"4'd0"}],"invariants":["n <= 4'd10","total <= 9'd3 * n"],"verilog":"module csa_budget_acc (
    input  wire       clk,
