{"cti_reasoning":"State S has a valid packet sitting in pipe stage 2 while the occupancy counter reads zero: it satisfies P because pipe[3] is clear (no packet is draining this cycle), but it violates R since popcount(pipe)=1 != o_inflight=0. With i_ce low the design sits in S forever; one enabled step with i_issue=0 shifts the marker into pipe[3] while the counter stays at 0 (no decrement, since the old pipe[3] was 0), producing pipe[3]=1 with o_inflight==0, which breaks P.","cti_state":[{"signal":"pipe","value":"4'b0100"},{"signal":"o_inflight","value":"3'd0"},{"signal":"o_drain","value":"1'b0"},{"signal":"rst","value":"1'b0"},{"signal":"i_ce","value":"1'b0"}],"invariants":["o_inflight == ({2'b0,pipe[0]} + {2'b0,pipe[1]} + {2'b0,pipe[2]} + {2'b0,pipe[3]})","o_inflight <= 3'd4"],"verilog":"// Fixed-latency packet capture pipeline with an in-flight occupancy tracker.
