{"cti_reasoning":"In state S the window is open and both error flags are still clear, so both assertions hold; but the latched sample temp_lat=200 is above T_HIGH while heater is still on, which violates the hysteresis consistency relation R. With ce low the design freezes in S for any number of cycles; the moment ce rises with the phase counter at its wrap value (phase==4) the divided enable fires, the error detector sees heater=1 together with temp_lat>T_HIGH and latches bad_hi=1 while win stays 1, breaking the property.","cti_state":[{"signal":"phase","value":"3'd4"},{"signal":"temp_lat","value":"8'd200"},{"signal":"heater","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"bad_hi","value":"1'b0"},{"signal":"bad_lo","value":"1'b0"},{"signal":"win","value":"1'b1"}],"invariants":["(temp_lat <= 8'd80) || (heater == 1'b0)","(temp_lat >= 8'd60) || (heater == 1'b1)","phase <= 3'd4"],"verilog":"module thermo_div_guard (
