{"cti_reasoning":"The state S has the FSM in the one-hot ISSUE_A state (4'b0010) but with occupancy already at 2, which satisfies P (occ <= 2, and every $past(occ) in the stalled window is 2) yet violates the R clause tying ISSUE_A to occ == 0; holding i_ce low lets the design sit in S indefinitely, and a single step with i_ce high takes the ISSUE_A branch, raising occ to 3 so the next $past(occ) check fails.","cti_state":[{"signal":"state","value":"4'b0010"},{"signal":"occ","value":"3'd2"},{"signal":"armed","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"pv","value":"1'b1"}],"invariants":["state == 4'b0001 || state == 4'b0010 || state == 4'b0100 || state == 4'b1000","!state[0] || occ == 3'd0","!state[1] || occ == 3'd0","!state[2] || occ == 3'd1","!state[3] || occ == 3'd2"],"verilog":"module onehot_issue_window (
    input  wire       clk,
