{"cti_reasoning":"The state win=8'b1000_0000 with ones=4'd4 satisfies P (the saturation flag needs ones==3, and 4!=3, so sat is low), but violates R because the population count of win is 1, not 4. With i_ce low the design sits in this state forever; one step with i_ce high and i_req low shifts the lone 1 out of the window (win becomes 8'd0, so win_empty rises) while ones decrements only to 3, raising sat, so sat && win_empty are both true with armed still set and P fails.","cti_state":[{"signal":"win","value":"8'b1000_0000"},{"signal":"ones","value":"4'd4"},{"signal":"armed","value":"1'b1"}],"invariants":["ones == (win[0]+win[1]+win[2]+win[3]+win[4]+win[5]+win[6]+win[7])","ones <= 4'd8"],"verilog":"// Sliding-window grant rate limiter for an accelerator DMA port.
// A shift register of the last 8 cycles of grants, plus a running
