{"cti_reasoning":"In state S the lockup counter zcnt is 0, so the property (on any rise of strobe, zcnt must be 0) holds — strobe is stable at 0 while i_ce is low, so the design can idle in S for any number of cycles. S violates R because the LFSR word is all zeros, which the real design can never reach. One enabled step from S keeps the LFSR stuck at zero (feedback of an all-zero word is zero), which makes the watchdog counter increment to 1 while the zero-nibble strobe goes 0->1, so $rose(strobe) is true in a cycle where zcnt == 1 and P fails.","cti_state":[{"signal":"lfsr","value":"8'h00"},{"signal":"zcnt","value":"4'd0"},{"signal":"strobe","value":"1'b0"},{"signal":"pv","value":"1'b1"}],"invariants":["lfsr != 8'h00"],"verilog":"module lfsr_lockup_watch (
