{"cti_reasoning":"State S has the window open (busy=1) with a registered valid index idx=2 whose bit is set in the shadow 'loaded' mask, so P holds, but the pending mask contains bits 3 and 5 that were never recorded in 'loaded', violating R's containment clause; with ce low the design sits in S forever, and one step with ce=1,pop=1 re-encodes the pending set to idx'=3 with idx_valid'=1 while loaded is unchanged, so loaded[3]==0 and P fails.","cti_state":[{"signal":"busy","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"idx_valid","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"idx","value":"3'd2"},{"signal":"pend","value":"8'b00101000"},{"signal":"loaded","value":"8'b00000100"}],"invariants":["(pend & ~loaded) == 8'b0","idx_valid == (pend != 8'b0)"],"verilog":"module strsearch_match_queue (
