{"cti_reasoning":"In state S the writer is busy with wcnt=3 but the countdown ttl has already reached 0, so the by-construction relation ttl == 8 - wcnt (while busy) is broken; P still holds there because err_r has not moved and the design can sit in S forever with ce low ($stable(busy) and $stable(err_r) both hold). Raising ce for one cycle takes the 'expired while busy' path, setting err_r from 0 to 1 while busy stays 1 (wcnt=3 is not the last word), so $stable(busy) is true but $stable(err_r) is false and P fails in the successor state.","cti_state":[{"signal":"busy","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"wcnt","value":"4'd3"},{"signal":"ttl","value":"4'd0"},{"signal":"err_r","value":"1'b0"},{"signal":"sel","value":"1'b0"},{"signal":"rsel","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"rcnt","value":"4'd0"},{"signal":"rvld","value":"1'b0"},{"signal":"pv","value":"1'b1"}],"invariants":["wcnt <= 4'd7","ttl <= 4'd8","rcnt <= 4'd7","!busy || (ttl == 4'd8 - wcnt)","rsel != sel"],"verilog":"// Ping-pong (double) buffer fill engine with a completion deadline counter.
